## Non-Mermaid description (accessible alternative)

The governed runtime executes a scientific task. Each step emits typed
events: a proposal, an action request and result, state snapshots and state
differences, evidence and verifier results, and belief records. A sealed
fault injector may perturb the execution; its truth is hidden from the
policy. All events flow into an append-only trace store. An independent
adjudicator, which never reads the policy's hidden state or self-report,
produces the terminal scientific outcome used for evaluation.
